# Background theory for the GeoNames slice: France and Germany declared
# disjoint.
#
# GeoNames publishes no disjointness.  The parties declare that nothing
# lies within both countries.  Disjointness implies distinctness, and it
# also settles containment: France lies within itself, so it cannot lie
# within Germany (KGC306).

@prefix bt:      <https://w3id.org/odrl-kb/background#> .
@prefix dcterms: <http://purl.org/dc/terms/> .

<https://w3id.org/odrl-kb/geonames-europe/siblings> a bt:BackgroundTheory ;
    dcterms:title "France and Germany declared disjoint"@en ;
    bt:generatedBy bt:PartyDeclaration ;
    bt:appliesTo <https://w3id.org/odrl-kb/geonames-europe> ;
    bt:pairCount 1 .
